Scaffold a detection rule.

␛[1m␛[4mUsage:␛[0m ␛[1mopentide new rule␛[0m [OPTIONS]

␛[1m␛[4mOptions:␛[0m
      ␛[1m--name␛[0m <NAME>
          Object name; the filename is its slug

      ␛[1m--platform␛[0m <PLATFORM>
          Add a configuration block for this platform (repeatable): sentinel, defender_for_endpoint, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops
          
          [possible values: sentinel, defender_for_endpoint, splunk, sentinel_one, crowdstrike, harfanglab, carbon_black_cloud, elastic, sysdig, bitdefender, graylog, exabeam, google_secops]

      ␛[1m--objective␛[0m <OBJECTIVE>
          UUID of the objective this rule implements (detection_model)

      ␛[1m--path␛[0m <PATH>
          File to write, or a folder to write it in (default: the family's objects folder)

      ␛[1m--help␛[0m
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide new rule --name "Suspicious LSASS Access" --platform sentinel --objective <objective-uuid>

